// c04_functio_typo.exsc
//
// Case c04. The mistake: `funtcio` typed for `functio`.
//
// Review reported: `1:9 EXS-E0201` + `3:1 EXS-E0201`, no fix. Verdict:
// "bad" -- no "did you mean `functio`?" suggestion despite this being a
// Levenshtein-1 hit in a closed 30-word keyword set (spec §8.4); one typo
// produces two diagnostics.
//
// Reconstruction: byte-faithful. Counting from the first byte of `publica`
// below, this file reproduces both `1:9 EXS-E0201` (the misspelt keyword
// itself) and `3:1 EXS-E0201` (the closing `}`, since with no `functio`
// recognised the whole body never parses as a function), both with
// `fix: null` -- exactly as reported.

publica funtcio maxima(a: u64) -> u64 {
    redde a;
}
